{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1569952877,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDEwNTU0NDE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3744","origin":"github"},"title":"Comparative conceptual benchmark implementations","message":"At present we have benchmarks that compare simultaneously present alternative implementations (e.g. `time_rev_createadd_to_dataset` vs `time_createadd_to_dataset`). It would be very useful to have conceptually congruent implementations that embody a kind of \"best of breed\" approach to solve a given task with a given version of the API. This would allow for adding a dedicated benchmark CI run to compare task performance between (major) release, rather than command performance (which is impossible whenever commands change semantics, or vanish ala `add()`). This would also capture high-level improvements by utilizing more flexible or more capable features and/or new command to solve a given task.","files":null}]}